{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>YHWH alone did guide him.</b> He led them in the wilderness alone and secure." "<b>and with Him no foreign god.</b> No power belonged to any one of the gods of the nations to show its might and wage war against them. And our Sages interpreted it of the future, and so Onkelos renders it. And I say: these are words of reproof — to call heaven and earth as witnesses, and let this song be for them as testimony that they are destined to betray, and will remember neither the former things He did for them nor the things to come that He is destined to do for them; therefore the matter must be settled here and there. And the entire subject turns on <b>Remember the days of old, consider the years of many generations</b> — thus He did for them, and thus He is destined to do for them; all this was for them as a remembrance."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:13.655080256Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}